# Keep contextual help docs in sync

When changing product behavior, keep the in-app help system fully updated in the same session.

## Required updates on feature change

If you create, modify, rename, or remove any user-facing feature/page/control:

1. Update `app/resources/js/src/data/appDocumentation.js`:
   - `summary` and `overview` for affected topics
   - `controls` (buttons, toggles, workflows, validations)
   - `concepts` (what numbers/states mean)
   - `related` links and route aliases/keywords
2. If routes changed, update mapping behavior in:
   - `app/resources/js/src/utils/documentationLinks.js`
   - route matching entries in `appDocumentation.js`
3. Keep docs accurate for add/change/delete:
   - Added feature → add/expand topic
   - Changed behavior → revise existing text
   - Removed feature → remove/replace stale docs references
4. Ensure docs stay practical and detailed (not one-line placeholders).
5. Update `implementation.md` to note the documentation-sync changes made.

## Validation

- Run frontend checks/build after substantial docs/schema edits.
- Never leave outdated help text that contradicts current UI behavior.
